In Go 1.21, the `for` loop variable `i` is reused across iterations, and the goroutine closures capture the variable itself, not the current value. By the time the goroutines actually run and call `fmt.Println(i)`, the loop has finished and `i` is `5`.

Fix it by passing the current value into the goroutine:

<solution language="go" verdict="fix">
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"sync"
)

func main() {
	var wg sync.WaitGroup
	for i := 0; i < 5; i++ {
		wg.Add(1)
		go func(n int) {
			defer wg.Done()
			fmt.Println(n)
		}(i)
	}
	wg.Wait()
}
</solution>

