message.content:
The main bug is this line:

```rust
if data[i] == max_val {
```

That compares the current element to the **best value found so far**, not to the **previous element**. A streak is consecutive equal values, so you need to compare `data[i]` with `data[i - 1]`.

There is also a second bug: the final streak is never checked after the loop ends. In `[2, 2, 1, 1, 1]`, the longest streak is at the end, so without a final check it is missed.

<solution language="rust" verdict="fix">
fn longest_streak(data: &Vec<i32>) -> (i32, usize) {
    let mut max_val = data[0];
    let mut max_count: usize = 1;
    let mut current_count: usize = 1;

    for i in 1..data.len() {
        if data[i] == data[i - 1] {
            current_count += 1;
        } else {
            if current_count > max_count {
                max_count = current_count;
                max_val = data[i - 1];
            }
            current_count = 1;
        }
    }

    if current_count > max_count {
        max_count = current_count;
        max_val = data[data.len() - 1];
    }

    (max_val, max_count)
}
</solution>

